What’s the difference between metrics, logs, and traces, and when do you start with each? 

metrics tell what is wrong 
traces show where it broke down
logs explain why it happened  

Metrics :-Numeric measurements of system health, like CPU usage, request counts, or error rates, aggregated over time. 
Setting up active alerts and monitoring long-term performance trends. 

Traces:- Visual maps that follow a single user request as it travels through multiple microservices, networks, and databases.  use case is Troubleshooting latency and mapping out complex dependencies. 

Logs:- Discrete, time-stamped text records of specific events, such as a stack trace or an "Order Processed" notification. use case is digging into the root cause of an error. 

